# kk: Encode indirect count draws into an ICB inside the render pass
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46361 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

```
vkCmdDraw*IndirectCount currently ends the render pass and unrolls the
draws in a compute pass. This MR encodes them into an indirect command
buffer from a vertex dispatch and executes it in the same render pass,
as planned in 0126f4388a5 ("kk: One MTL4CommandBuffer per
VkCommandBuffer").

* The first commit folds the sample ID and position in single-sample
  fragment shaders, so they no longer run per sample. The ICB path
  excludes fragment shaders that read the sample ID, so this also lets
  more draws use it.
* The second commit adds the ICB path. The previous path is kept for the
  cases listed in the commit message.
* The third commit Adds visibility argument to barrier.

Tested on an Apple M5 Pro with macOS 27.2. Vulkan CTS: no regressions
against main on 79,312 cases, and no failures or Metal API validation
messages on the indirect count groups. Other GPUs and macOS 26 were not
tested.

Enshrouded under Wine, average FPS over three A/B runs against main:
* Barrier and ICB commits only: 30.5 to 37.4, +22.7%
* All three commits: 30.3 to 38.9, +28.5%
```
